{
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(git push origin main)",
      "Bash(git push origin main:claude/worker-brief-fable-vnnuv8)",
      "Bash(git push origin main:blinded-fable)",
      "Bash(git push -q origin main)",
      "Bash(git push -q origin main:claude/worker-brief-fable-vnnuv8)",
      "Bash(git push -q origin main:blinded-fable)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/home/user/fortress-transcripts-blinded/scripts/backup.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/home/user/fortress/.claude/hooks/model-check.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/home/user/fortress/.claude/hooks/git-check-off.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/home/user/fortress/.claude/hooks/git-check-off.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "printf \"%s\\n\" \"{\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\":{\\\"hookEventName\\\":\\\"SessionStart\\\",\\\"additionalContext\\\":\\\"This session was just compacted. Before anything else, check the serving model by running explorations/coordinator/tools/model-now.sh, and with the get_session tool and no session_id only if it prints nothing; if it is neither Opus nor Fable, tell the curator first. Then boot: load the fortress-repo skill, then the coordinator skill, with the Skill tool, so that each is its current version and the worker skill's core comes first, and follow the coordinator skill's section The boot (explorations/coordinator/FACTS.md whole, in pages, POSITIONS.md and INDEX.md; check-index.sh; the first section of explorations/coordinator/PLAN.md; the boot note explorations/coordinator/BOOT.md, then the held list explorations/coordinator/HELD.md; git log; and for a running batch the skill's batch part). Do not boot from a copy of the skill shown from before the compaction: it can be an older version, whose parts no longer exist. Only then continue what the summary describes, and say that the boot was done.\\\"}}\""
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

